Z||000000||hefty||10-17-1999||06:05 PM||||I've had my Fiero for about a month now. What a car. I've owned muscle cars ( '69 road runner, '66 and two '70 Lemans a few camaro's '78 datson z list goes on ) and radical off road (4x4) machines. My Fiero is a keeper ! It's an '87 GT v6 5 speed. 85k on it. I'm in love with almost every thing about this auto. I'm looking to get around 260hp, should I consider sticking with the 2.8L ? I want to keep it a 6 cyl. Would it be easier to go w/3.4L ? how would stock trans. hold up ?<p>[This message has been edited by hefty (edited 10-17-1999).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||88 Fiero||10-17-1999||08:19 PM||||hefty...I'm glad you like the Fiero's ...if you would consider to rebuilt your 2.8..go with the 3.4 camaro block...it's a very good block and your car still would look stock..another reason why a 3.4 is when you decide to install a turbo kit..that's where the fun starts...or install a Northstar engine and see if anyone can hang on to you whether it's a 1/4 mile or curves...||||reg||1
